    "body": "Okay, so I asked around, checked the implementation, and I'm now confident that option 1 matches our behavior. I tried to spec that, except the backpressure thing. I think that one is more of the description for suspend/resume (and thus kinda out of scope of this PR).\r\n\r\nEdit: The PR somehow copied \"Let buffer an empty buffer that can have ... appended to it\" from [infra](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#forgiving-base64-decode), and used \"append\" and \"extract\" against that without the definitions. Infra doesn't really define \"append\" against buffer either, so maybe it's okay?",
